{pad:meta title='Toys'/}

<p>{app:tag 'toy:life'/} puts a small live simulation or visual toy on the page - a Game of Life, a flock of
birds, a double pendulum, falling sand, the Mandelbrot set. The server checks the options it is
given and writes its frame; the toy's script, written once per page, runs it. There are
{pad:echo php:count(padToyTypes())/} of them - every toy is a file of <code>pad/subs/games/toys/types/</code>, and the
<a href="../toys/">toys</a> application shows them all.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/toys_1'/}

<h2>Select a kind</h2>

<p>Use <code>{pad:open/}toy:life/{pad:close/}</code> to select the kind. Every toy can be touched: draw cells, drag a bob,
throw a planet, stir the current - and has its controls below it, each with a label, and the keys
it reads while it has the focus.</p>

<h2>Patterns and rules between the tags</h2>

<p>A Game of Life takes a pattern of its own between its tags, a row a line - <code>O</code> alive,
<code>.</code> dead - and an L-system its own rules: the word to start with, the turn, and a line per
letter that is rewritten. They are taken as written, before the level walks them - a field or a tag
there is not filled in.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/toys_2'/}

<h2>Options</h2>

<p>Each toy has a few options of its own - the algorithm and the bars of a sort, the birds of a flock,
the rule of an ant - checked on the server: a number out of its bounds or a word the toy does not
know is named under the strict check.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/toys_3'/}

<h2>Waiting, and the same start every time</h2>

<p><code>seed=</code> makes what a toy picks at random the same on every load - the scattered cells, the
birds, the shells of the fireworks. <code>paused</code> has a toy wait for its Play button, and every
toy waits when the visitor asks for reduced motion; a drawing toy then shows its figure finished,
as a still picture.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/toys_4'/}

<ul>
  <li>A toy holds while the page is hidden or the toy is scrolled out of view, and goes on where it
  was when it is seen again; its root carries <code>data-state</code> - <code>playing</code>,
  <code>paused</code> or <code>held</code>.</li>
  <li>The colours are custom properties on <code>.pad-toy</code> - <code>--pad-toy-accent</code>,
  <code>--pad-toy-canvas</code>, <code>--pad-toy-night</code> and their like - with light and dark
  defaults; a canvas cannot paint them as they are, so the script resolves them for the page's scheme
  and again when it changes.</li>
  <li>The script carries the CSP nonce, as the interactive tags' scripts do, and a toy a fragment or a
  live region brings later starts as well.</li>
</ul>
